            <ArticleTitle>Cross-reactions to desoximetasone and mometasone furoate in a patient with multiple topical corticosteroid allergies.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>147-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 60-year-old man developed a bullous contact dermatitis after topical corticosteroid treatment of dermatitis on his lower leg. Subsequent patch testing showed cross-reactions to numerous group B and group D corticosteroids as well as cross-reactions to group C desoximetasone and group D1 mometasone furoate. His patch-test result was negative for the group A corticosteroids hydrocortisone and tixocortol pivalate. We discuss the uncommon finding of cross-reactions to desoximetasone and mometasone furoate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
